// Realm conformance gate — provider fixture A.
//
// A lone provider of the coeffect key `kv`, isolated into realm("other").
// It is compiled as its OWN unit: revl's linker rejects two same-realm
// providers of one key at admission (G2, examples/rejections/
// v2_same_realm_conflict.rvl), so to exercise the RUNTIME's enforcement the
// two providers must reach the runtime without being co-linked. The bodies
// are stateless and Int-shaped so the one fixture lowers on every tier,
// including the cordis-wasm substrate.
//
// Contract (docs/design-v2-realms.md):
//   "A realm label is a static string literal. Equal strings = same realm"
//   "G2 becomes per-(key, realm): ... the same realm is the conflict, and
//    the error names the realm."

service Kv {
  fn get(k: Int) -> Int
  fn set(k: Int, v: Int)
}

component SharedStoreOther provides kv: Kv {
  isolate kv in realm("other")
  provide kv {
    fn get(k) = 0
    fn set(k, v) { }
  }
}
